  "name": "Babyfur Con",
  "shortName": "BFC",
  "description": "Babyfur Con (BFC) is an annual furry convention in Santa Cruz, California, for the babyfur and AB/DL members of the fandom. It began as Cub Con, a small event inside Biggest Little Fur Con in May 2019, created by Nacho Husky, Kago and Panda, and its meet-and-greet drew over 150 attendees. In 2020 it became Virtual Babyfur Con, held on Zoom with more than 400 attendees from over 20 countries, and its proceeds helped establish the Partnership for Artists and Creative Individuals (PACI), the organization that runs the convention. The first in-person Babyfur Con was held October 6 to 9, 2023, with the hotel booked entirely for the event. The hotel is not publicly named to protect attendee privacy, and a registration lottery is used because of the small attendance cap.",
